  "title": "Universal highly arc transitive digraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "An alternating walk in a digraph is a walk $v_0,e_1,v_1,\\ldots,v_m$ so that the vertex $v_i$ is either the head of both $e_i$ and $e_{i+1}$ or the tail of both $e_i$ and $e_{i+1}$ for every $1 \\le i \\le m-1$. A digraph is universal if for every pair of edges $e,f$, there is an alternating walk containing both $e$ and $f$\n\nQuestion Does there exist a locally finite highly arc transitive digraph which is universal?",
    "sha256": "52ffb391dad9951ff40398e89a31023a0d38703f964a4a7f187aaf098b8877e4",
